        {
          "id": "p3-1",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Did you make notes while you were watching the performances of Romeo and Juliet, Gemma?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-2",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yes, I did. I found it quite hard though. I kept getting too involved in the play."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-3",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Me too. I ended up not taking notes. I wrote down my impressions when I got home. Do you mind if I check a few things with you? In case I’ve missed anything. And I’ve also got some questions about our assignment."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-4",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "No, it’s good to talk things through. I may have missed things too."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-5",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "OK great. So first of all, I’m not sure how much information we should include in our reviews."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-6",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Right. Well, I don’t think we need to describe what happens. Especially as Romeo and Juliet is one of Shakespeare’s most well-known plays."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-7",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Yeah, everyone knows the story. In an essay we’d focus on the poetry and Shakespeare’s use of imagery etc., but that isn’t really relevant in a review. We’re supposed to focus on how effective this particular production is."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-8",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Mmm. We should say what made it a success or a failure."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-9",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "And part of that means talking about the emotional impact the performance had on us. I think that’s important."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-10",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yes. And we should definitely mention how well the director handled important bits of the play - like when Romeo climbs onto Juliet’s balcony."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-11",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "And the fight between Mercutio and Tybalt."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-12",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yes. It would also be interesting to mention the theatre space and how the director used it but I don’t think we’ll have space in 800 words."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-13",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "No. OK. That all sounds quite straightforward."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-14",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "So what about The Emporium Theatre’s production of the play?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-15",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "I thought some things worked really well but there were some problems too."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-16",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Yeah. What about the set, for example?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-17",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "I think it was visually really stunning. I’d say that was probably the most memorable thing about this production."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-18",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "You’re right. The set design was really amazing, but actually I have seen similar ideas used in other productions."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-19",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "What about the lighting? Some of the scenes were so dimly lit it was quite hard to see."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-20",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "I didn’t dislike it. It helped to change the mood of the quieter scenes."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-21",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "That’s a good point."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-22",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "What did you think of the costumes?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-23",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "I was a bit surprised by the contemporary dress, I must say."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-24",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Yeah - I think it worked well, but I had assumed it would be more conventional."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-25",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Me too. I liked the music at the beginning and I thought the musicians were brilliant, but I thought they were wasted because the music didn’t have much impact in Acts 2 and 3."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-26",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Yes - that was a shame."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-27",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "One problem with this production was that the actors didn’t deliver the lines that well. They were speaking too fast."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-28",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "It was a problem I agree, but I thought it was because they weren’t speaking loudly enough - especially at key points in the play."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-29",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "I actually didn’t have a problem with that."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-30",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "It’s been an interesting experience watching different versions of Romeo and Juliet, hasn’t it?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-31",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Definitely. It’s made me realise how relevant the play still is."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-32",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Right. I mean a lot’s changed since Shakespeare’s time, but in many ways nothing’s changed. There are always disagreements and tension between teenagers and their parents."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-33",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yes, that’s something all young people can relate to - more than the violence and the extreme emotions in the play."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-34",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "How did you find watching it in translation?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-35",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Really interesting. I expected to find it more challenging, but I could follow the story pretty well."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-36",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "I stopped worrying about not being able to understand all the words and focused on the actors’ expressions. The ending was pretty powerful."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-37",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yes. That somehow intensified the emotion for me."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-38",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Did you know Shakespeare’s been translated into more languages than any other writer?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-39",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "What’s the reason for his international appeal, do you think?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-40",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "I was reading that it’s because his plays are about basic themes that people everywhere are familiar with."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-41",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "Yeah, and they can also be understood on different levels. The characters have such depth."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-42",
          "speaker": "Ed",
          "text": "Right - which allows directors to experiment and find new angles."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-43",
          "speaker": "Gemma",
          "text": "That’s really important because …"
        }
