        {
          "id": "p4-2",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "Others, like the Arctic Tern, travel more than 25,000 miles seasonally between the northern and southern poles. Bird migration has been studied over many centuries through a variety of observations."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-3",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "But until relatively recently, where birds went to in the winter was considered something of a mystery. The lack of modern science and technology led to many theories that we now recognize as error-filled and even somewhat amusing."
